@page "/async"

<PageTitle>Async rules</PageTitle>
<h1>Async rules</h1>
<p>Type "admin" and pause: each keystroke starts the check immediately (the 600ms delay simulates a server call), shows a pending state, and a new keystroke cancels the in-flight check.</p>

<TeachingPanel CodeFiles="@(new[] { "Handle.cs", "AsyncRules.razor", "AsyncRules.razor.cs" })">
    <Rules>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Username</strong> and <strong>Display name</strong> — checked for uniqueness asynchronously while you type (a 600&nbsp;ms delay stands in for the server). Taken usernames: <code>admin</code>, <code>root</code>, <code>formidable</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Username</strong> — also required at submit.</li>
        </ul>
    </Rules>
    <TryIt>
        <ol>
            <li>Type <code>admin</code> and pause — a spinner and "checking…" appear on that field only, then the taken message lands.</li>
            <li>Type quickly — each keystroke cancels the in-flight check; only the final value gets a verdict.</li>
            <li>Type in Display name — its indicator runs independently; the pending state is scoped to the field being edited.</li>
            <li>Clear Username and submit — the required rule blocks.</li>
        </ol>
    </TryIt>
</TeachingPanel>

<FormidableForm Model="_handle" OnValidSubmit="HandleValid">
    <FormSummary />

    <FormidableField For="() => _handle.Username" Context="field">
        <div class="field">
            <label>Username <FormidableInputText For="() => _handle.Username" @bind-Value="_handle.Username" UpdateOn="InputUpdateMode.OnInput" /></label>
            @if (field.State.IsValidating)
            {
                <em role="status">checking…</em>
            }
        </div>
        <FieldMessage For="() => _handle.Username" />
    </FormidableField>

    <FormidableField For="() => _handle.DisplayName" Context="field">
        <div class="field">
            <label>Display name <FormidableInputText For="() => _handle.DisplayName" @bind-Value="_handle.DisplayName" UpdateOn="InputUpdateMode.OnInput" /></label>
            @if (field.State.IsValidating)
            {
                <em role="status">checking…</em>
            }
        </div>
        <FieldMessage For="() => _handle.DisplayName" />
    </FormidableField>

    <div class="actions">
        <button type="submit">Submit</button>
    </div>
</FormidableForm>

<p role="status">@_status</p>

<p><small>The pending flag is scoped to the field being edited during a live pass — type in Username or Display name and only that field's "checking…" indicator shows, not both.</small></p>
